WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.350
(audience cheering)
- I will tell you,

00:00:01.350 --> 00:00:02.800
I have interviewed so many people.

00:00:02.800 --> 00:00:04.670
I'm so lucky, this job has been,

00:00:04.670 --> 00:00:06.950
I've been so fortunate to
get to meet a lot of people

00:00:06.950 --> 00:00:08.900
that I love and inspire me.

00:00:08.900 --> 00:00:10.670
I have been asking my producer

00:00:10.670 --> 00:00:12.370
when this show is going to happen,

00:00:12.370 --> 00:00:15.580
for I don't know how long,
and I loved the film.

00:00:15.580 --> 00:00:18.790
It was so good, it was so moving.

00:00:18.790 --> 00:00:22.210
I laughed, I cried, I was inspired.

00:00:22.210 --> 00:00:23.043
It was thought provoking.

00:00:23.043 --> 00:00:25.760
There were so many things
happening with the film.

00:00:25.760 --> 00:00:27.360
And it's great to have you here.

00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:28.835
Thank you for taking the time.

00:00:28.835 --> 00:00:29.668
- Thank you for having us.
(audience clapping)

00:00:29.668 --> 00:00:31.797
- You're so busy winning awards.

00:00:31.797 --> 00:00:32.630
- Thank you, thank you so much.

00:00:32.630 --> 00:00:35.150
- But it's great to see you again Marlee.

00:00:35.150 --> 00:00:36.540
Thank you for coming back.

00:00:36.540 --> 00:00:39.500
- So I was counting the days

00:00:39.500 --> 00:00:40.850
when I was gonna come
back to see you again.

00:00:40.850 --> 00:00:43.823
Thank you for having us here,
and I love your show so much.

00:00:43.823 --> 00:00:45.670
I love you, I Love you, I love you.

00:00:45.670 --> 00:00:47.560
And speaking about, I love you,

00:00:47.560 --> 00:00:49.130
we are giving you a gift here.

00:00:49.130 --> 00:00:51.150
- [Kelly] Oh? What?

00:00:51.150 --> 00:00:53.150
- Here, this is for you.
- What?

00:00:53.150 --> 00:00:55.640
- This is a very special gift,

00:00:55.640 --> 00:00:57.343
that was made for you,

00:00:58.831 --> 00:01:01.240
I'm giving to you, by my best friend,

00:01:01.240 --> 00:01:02.690
her name is Alexis Kashar.

00:01:02.690 --> 00:01:04.557
- [Kelly] My makeup
artist is gonna hate me.

00:01:04.557 --> 00:01:06.257
(Kelly laughing)
That's so sweet!

00:01:07.160 --> 00:01:10.390
- And it's a sign for I
love you, it's a pendant.

00:01:10.390 --> 00:01:14.610
- That's so sweet.
(audience clapping)

00:01:14.610 --> 00:01:15.483
So why I'm crying-

00:01:15.483 --> 00:01:17.980
- It's a line of jewelry
called RoseBYANDER,

00:01:17.980 --> 00:01:21.130
so that's the name of the
jewelry and it's just to,

00:01:21.130 --> 00:01:22.200
I love you
- I love it.

00:01:22.200 --> 00:01:23.490
One of a kind special jewelry.

00:01:23.490 --> 00:01:25.060
- It's amazing 'cause
it's coming from you.

00:01:25.060 --> 00:01:27.000
It's also a very special
meaning, side note for me

00:01:27.000 --> 00:01:29.660
and my daughter that I won't say on-air

00:01:29.660 --> 00:01:30.650
because I'll cry.

00:01:30.650 --> 00:01:31.990
But anyway, there's something special

00:01:31.990 --> 00:01:33.370
with this sign with me and my kid as well.

00:01:33.370 --> 00:01:34.310
So this is very beautiful.

00:01:34.310 --> 00:01:38.230
Thank you so much!
(audience clapping)

00:01:38.230 --> 00:01:41.280
Had any of y'all met before this movie?

00:01:41.280 --> 00:01:42.970
- Yeah, we did, we knew each other.

00:01:42.970 --> 00:01:43.803
We all knew each other.

00:01:43.803 --> 00:01:44.640
The three of us knew each other

00:01:44.640 --> 00:01:47.320
but actually working as
intensely as we did on this film,

00:01:47.320 --> 00:01:48.980
no, we didn't actually.

00:01:48.980 --> 00:01:51.610
So I'm so honored to have
worked with the two of them.

00:01:51.610 --> 00:01:54.180
They're so talented deaf actors,

00:01:54.180 --> 00:01:57.420
and it was really more
special to have Amelia

00:01:57.420 --> 00:01:59.020
on board with us as well.

00:01:59.020 --> 00:02:00.290
This is the perfect cast.

00:02:00.290 --> 00:02:02.075
You'll never see a more perfect cast.

00:02:02.075 --> 00:02:04.083
(audience cheering)

00:02:04.083 --> 00:02:06.180
- I could not agree more.

00:02:06.180 --> 00:02:08.510
It was, and I've never seen it on film.

00:02:08.510 --> 00:02:10.160
That's why I think this
is so important in film.

00:02:10.160 --> 00:02:11.680
I've never seen a full cast like this.

00:02:11.680 --> 00:02:13.610
I never really had to watch

00:02:13.610 --> 00:02:15.700
or pay attention in a different way.

00:02:15.700 --> 00:02:17.490
It was such a beautiful

00:02:17.490 --> 00:02:21.340
and needed experience that I
did not know that I needed.

00:02:21.340 --> 00:02:23.410
And I did not know that
American Sign Language

00:02:23.410 --> 00:02:25.180
it's so passionate.

00:02:25.180 --> 00:02:26.780
It's a passionate language.

00:02:26.780 --> 00:02:29.920
I mean, it's a full body you're
not just using your voice.

00:02:29.920 --> 00:02:31.100
It's a full body experience

00:02:31.100 --> 00:02:32.650
of how deeply hurt you are,
- Right.

00:02:32.650 --> 00:02:34.780
- Or how deeply in love you are,

00:02:34.780 --> 00:02:36.620
or, you know, frustrated you are.

00:02:36.620 --> 00:02:38.890
It was just such an
amazing thing to watch.

00:02:38.890 --> 00:02:42.660
- Exactly, it's because it's two things.

00:02:42.660 --> 00:02:46.910
We are able to express ourselves,

00:02:46.910 --> 00:02:49.460
our language within deaf culture,

00:02:49.460 --> 00:02:51.500
but we're also damn good actors.

00:02:51.500 --> 00:02:52.440
So that's all you can say,

00:02:52.440 --> 00:02:53.289
I mean, when you do it then you sell.

00:02:53.289 --> 00:02:55.511
- [Kelly] Yeah! Yeah!
(audience cheering)

00:02:55.511 --> 00:03:00.511
But, this movie is one that most people

00:03:01.610 --> 00:03:03.790
the majority of people
probably aren't accustomed to.

00:03:03.790 --> 00:03:05.530
I mean, there are all
other kinds of movies,

00:03:05.530 --> 00:03:07.200
and those are all wonderful films

00:03:07.200 --> 00:03:09.390
but this is unique and
it's special in itself,

00:03:09.390 --> 00:03:11.840
and the fact that there's so
many different levels operating

00:03:11.840 --> 00:03:14.160
at the same time in the
film, people will connect

00:03:14.160 --> 00:03:16.310
to whatever level that
they're watching in the film

00:03:16.310 --> 00:03:17.810
whether it's fishing, or songs,

00:03:17.810 --> 00:03:20.690
or music, or sign language, or schools,

00:03:20.690 --> 00:03:23.910
or teenage life, or family
life, it's all in one film.

00:03:23.910 --> 00:03:25.400
It's the entire package.

00:03:25.400 --> 00:03:28.050
It's a beautiful, wonderful
package for the audience.

